@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy and Data";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    MotoGarage is a motorcycle garage management application
    developed for the SoftUni ASP.NET Fundamentals course.
    This page describes the data used by the demonstration application.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Information stored</h2>

<p>The application stores information entered into its forms:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Customer first names, last names, phone numbers and optional email addresses.</li>
    <li>Motorcycle details and their associated customers.</li>
    <li>Service types, service dates, prices and optional notes.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">How information is used</h2>

<p>
    Information is used to manage customers, motorcycles and service
    history, and to calculate dashboard counts and service values.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Data storage</h2>

<p>
    Application records are stored in the SQL Server database
    configured for this installation. The default development
    configuration uses SQL Server Express LocalDB.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Access to records</h2>

<p>
    This demonstration version does not include user accounts or
    access restrictions. Anyone who can access the running application
    can use its record management features.
    Use fictional customer information when testing or demonstrating it.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Editing and deleting information</h2>

<p>
    Records can be edited or deleted through the application.
    A customer with linked motorcycles cannot be deleted.
    Deleting a motorcycle also deletes its associated service records.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Daily and monthly values</h2>

<p>
    Daily and monthly service values are calculated using service dates.
    Starting a new day or month does not delete previous records.
</p>